and that's what is about.

264
00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:52.420
Yeah, did the kid who originally challenged you?

265
00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:54.460
Do you know who that, do you have his name

266
00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:55.293
and stuff like that?

267
00:11:55.293 --> 00:11:56.650
We put it on social media.

268
00:11:57.632 --> 00:11:58.465
I saw that.
The team is probably

269
00:11:58.465 --> 00:11:59.867
looking for him, that he is going to--

270
00:11:59.867 --> 00:12:02.040
I know, I feel like

271
00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:03.933
you need to have a Tet attack with that kid.

272
00:12:03.933 --> 00:12:06.016
(laughs)

273
00:12:07.110 --> 00:12:09.680
And it is really,

274
00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:13.440
this moment is exciting for so many reasons.

275
00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:18.440
And my team watched me evolve, just as a human being,

276
00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:22.053
this evolution that I'm going through,

277
00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:25.650
I'm nowhere near where I'm going to end,

278
00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:27.300
but I'm evolving in so much.

279
00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.200
And it was never about the destiny.

280
00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:32.320
My team heard me say this over and over again.

281
00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:34.770
It was never about do I become mayor?

282
00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:35.630
It's the journey.

283
00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:39.300
All I know is this journey is preparing me

284
00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:41.450
for what my real purpose is

285
00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:43.257
and the hurdles I had to go through.

286
00:12:43.257 --> 00:12:46.540
And this was a tough, tough, tough journey.

287
00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:49.190
We had incoming coming from all over the place,

288
00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:51.960
but we remained, we had a motto,

289
00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:56.891
stay focused, no distractions and grind, that was it.

290
00:12:56.891 --> 00:12:57.724
(chuckles)

291
00:12:57.724 --> 00:12:58.557
Yeah, I asked you right

292
00:12:58.557 --> 00:13:00.740
before we started recording, like how you feeling,

293
00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:03.550
and you're like, you gotta stay grounded.

294
00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:05.580
I can't fly too high.

295
00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:07.260
But you got a lot coming at you right now

296
00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:09.550
and I can't imagine what that's gonna look like.

297
00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:12.523
I mean, at this point, New York City is 70% Democrat,

298
00:13:15.074 --> 00:13:16.750
it's not a foregone conclusion,

299
00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:20.180
but in all likelihood you'll be the mayor.

300
00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:23.200
And in that situation,

301
00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:26.710
there's gonna be all kinds of insanity swirling around you.

302
00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:30.380
Like how do you stay grounded with that job?

303
00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:32.743
By being true to yourself.

304
00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:35.937
I know there are things I'm able to do

305
00:13:35.937 --> 00:13:38.980
and things I am not able to do.

306
00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:40.770
And just remain committed,

307
00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:44.700
wake up every day with the same focus that I've have had.

308
00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:48.520
You can't invent yourself a day one as being mayor

309
00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:50.360
if you didn't have those same practices

310
00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:52.030
while you were going through life.

311
00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:57.030
And so, growing up in South Jamaica Queens,

312
00:13:57.070 --> 00:14:00.440
mom moving us there from Brownsville,

313
00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:02.950
going through my entire educational experience,

314
00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:05.370
cry myself to sleep I mean, literally,

315
00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:07.680
of why can't learn, why I'm in the classroom

316
00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:12.010
and I'm being bullied as the dumb kid and getting Ds,

317
00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:13.470
no matter how hard I tried

318
00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:15.670
and being told by my teachers I was lazy.

319
00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:16.920
I know for getting third grade

320
00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:19.350
one teacher smacking me so hard,

321
00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:22.390
that it left a hand print on my face

322
00:14:22.390 --> 00:14:23.640
because they thought that

323
00:14:24.690 --> 00:14:26.090
I just didn't put in enough effort,

324
00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.730
but I was trying every night I was grinding.

325
00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:31.190
And it wasn't until I got into college,

326
00:14:31.190 --> 00:14:34.860
overheard a documentary, a learning disabilities.

327
00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:37.217
And I said, wow, do I have a learning disability?

328
00:14:37.217 --> 00:14:40.480
You got took out the documentary and realized that I did.

329
00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:42.910
And I was able to overcome that learning disability.

330
00:14:42.910 --> 00:14:44.500
Dyslexia or what was it?

331
00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:46.990
It was a combination of ADD and dyslexia.

332
00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:48.670
It was a combination of the two.

333
00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:50.800
So, I was in pretty bad shape.

334
00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:55.703
And I went from a D student to on the Dean's list.

335
00:14:56.860 --> 00:15:01.550
And it was amazing that I was undiagnosed

336
00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:04.060
and my mother not understanding that.

337
00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:05.750
And I still think today that my brother

338
00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:09.050
is dealing with bipolar that was never diagnosed.

339
00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:11.960
And because he never had was lucky

340
00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:14.200
like I was lucky to hear it,

341
00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:18.040
his pathway went totally different from my pathway.

342
00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:22.130
But imagine how many children never had that luck

343
00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:25.410
and they still are suffering from the outcomes.

344
00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:29.700
Yeah, just one of the many epidemics

345
00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:32.370
that we're dealing with right now, mental health.

346
00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:36.040
Especially in the wake of COVID with depression, anxiety,

347
00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:37.410
stress, all the pressures

348
00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:39.400
that everyday people are shouldering,

349
00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:42.060
just trying to pay the bills, make through the day.

350
00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:46.080
That's right and we no longer believe,

351
00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:50.290
that's why this race was important on so many levels.

352
00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:55.290
And that's why the campaign was not only built on a strategy

353
00:15:56.330 --> 00:16:01.300
of how to win, but a strategy of how to tell a story

354
00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:05.400
of the perfectly imperfect human being.

355
00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.102
I am so flawed, man.

356
00:16:07.102 --> 00:16:09.660
(laughs)

357
00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:12.290
It's refreshing if we say that.

358
00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:17.020
My campaign guru, Nathan.

359
00:16:17.020 --> 00:16:19.284
He said, "Man, we supposed to be in last place."

360
00:16:19.284 --> 00:16:21.240
(laughs)

361
00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:25.160
Because I am so flawed as a person.

362
00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:30.160
And I wanted to put my flawed persona on Broadway.

363
00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:34.740
I'm wondering everyone who had a learning disability,

364
00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:36.500
everyone who's dealing with diabetes,

365
00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:38.590
everyone who was ever bullied,

366
00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:42.060
everyone who was arrested and beat by police.

367
00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:44.080
I want everyone to see like, listen man,

368
00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:46.592
this guy is able to become the mayor.

369
00:16:46.592 --> 00:16:47.425
(laughs)

370
00:16:47.425 --> 00:16:50.040
Well, I think it's a breath of fresh air

371
00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:52.670
because we've developed this expectation,

372
00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:55.270
of how a politician speaks

373
00:16:55.270 --> 00:16:56.930
and the way they deliver their message.

374
00:16:56.930 --> 00:16:59.260
And these carefully crafted stories

375
00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:02.030
that are meant to check certain boxes

376
00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:05.980
and we've become, inoculated against that.

377
00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:08.490
And there is this thirst, this hunger

378
00:17:08.490 --> 00:17:10.010
for something real and something true.

379
00:17:10.010 --> 00:17:11.290
It goes back to what I was saying earlier,

380
00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:15.010
this idea of people know when something is real

381
00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.840
and when it's crafted, when it's manufactured.

382
00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:19.440
Right and that's the greatest gift

383
00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:21.690
I can give New Yorkers,

384
00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:24.720
which I'm hoping cascade throughout the entire country.

385
00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:28.550
Our NOAA knows a lie in what's real.

386
00:17:28.550 --> 00:17:31.060
And we have stopped listening to ourselves.

387
00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:36.060
We know, your spirit won't allow you to accept a lie.

388
00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:39.490
My message resonated with people

389
00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:43.100
because they felt the authentic approach of it.

390
00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:46.320
We carried them, we carried every New York is five Boroughs,

391
00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:50.573
we carry four Boroughs in the city of all ethnicities.

392
00:17:50.573 --> 00:17:52.200
(laughs)

393
00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:55.590
And that was a joy of this race,

394
00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:56.813
because I started to see--

395
00:17:56.813 --> 00:17:58.120
And you know an under dog candidate

396
00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:01.460
kind of creeping your way up or like sneaking past

397
00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:05.483
some bigger names along the way.

398
00:18:05.483 --> 00:18:08.370
And all the shenanigans with the,

399
00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:10.730
all the stuff that got baked into the account

400
00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:11.563
and all of that--

401
00:18:11.563 --> 00:18:12.396
Yes, yes.

402
00:18:12.396 --> 00:18:13.481
There you are man, swinging.

403
00:18:13.481 --> 00:18:15.930
Yes, and it feels good.

404
00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:18.610
And we never, there was never a time

405
00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:21.860
that the team felt as though we couldn't do it.

406
00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:24.900
Never, all we knew we had to do.

407
00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:26.760
Rachel you agree with that?

408
00:18:26.760 --> 00:18:27.600
What you saying right here.

409
00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:31.150
We said to put one foot in front of the other,

410
00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:33.900
that's all we did every day.

411
00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:35.313
We had to raise $11 million.

412
00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:41.000
Think about our astronomical is, $11 million.

413
00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:44.240
Where does a kid from Besta I get $11 million from,

414
00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:46.530
but we just did one fundraiser at a time,

415
00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:49.390
could have been five people, they're writing checks for $10.

416
00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:51.060
We took it and said, thank you.

417
00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:53.209
And then they will call 10 more friends.

418
00:18:53.209 --> 00:18:54.042
(chuckles)

419
00:18:54.042 --> 00:18:55.340
So what do you make of that,

420
00:18:55.340 --> 00:18:59.300
as somebody of this humble upbringing,

421
00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:02.500
who's come so far in your life and achieve so much?

422
00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:05.440
When you reflect on that, what are the lessons?

423
00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:08.200
What are the principles that you've organized

424
00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:12.010
your life around that have allowed you to excel?

425
00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:14.530
We had a rock that we use to hold

426
00:19:14.530 --> 00:19:15.770
that said believe.

427
00:19:15.770 --> 00:19:18.963
And after every event, we will have everyone touch the rock,

428
00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:23.560
because I believe that you just,

429
00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:26.430
as your fingerprints leave your DNA,

430
00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:28.480
your fingerprint of belief.

431
00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:31.080
I believe it leaves a DNA on everything.

432
00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:32.750
The people we come in contact with,

433
00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:35.270
if they believe their DNA of belief

434
00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:37.320
is going to impact you as well.

435
00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:40.910
And we wanted people to start believing in themselves.

436
00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:45.700
And we really believe that we created this,

437
00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:48.980
just this energy of people, of all ethnic groups,

438
00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:51.470
different languages and different cultures.

439
00:19:51.470 --> 00:19:53.246
They just believed.

440
00:19:53.246 --> 00:19:54.079
(chuckles)

441
00:19:54.079 --> 00:19:54.912
That's cool man.

442
00:19:54.912 --> 00:19:56.560
I got to tell you, like looking at you,

443
00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:58.305
you don't look a day over 40.

444
00:19:58.305 --> 00:19:59.560
(laughs)

445
00:19:59.560 --> 00:20:01.583
You really don't, I mean you 61.

446
00:20:03.083 --> 00:20:03.916
Yes.

447
00:20:03.916 --> 00:20:08.020
61, I mean, like just the model of vitality.

448
00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:10.810
So I do wanna get back to the health thing.

449
00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:12.080
Like, let's talk about that.

450
00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:13.530
'Cause that's a crazy story.

451
00:20:13.530 --> 00:20:16.430
And I feel like you mentioned earlier,

452
00:20:16.430 --> 00:20:19.350
the importance of telling a story, how you tell a story,

453
00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:21.130
the story that you are telling.

454
00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:24.350
There's so many issues that face New York,

455
00:20:24.350 --> 00:20:27.760
those require your focus and your attention.

456
00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:29.610
The health piece is a big piece.

457
00:20:29.610 --> 00:20:33.860
I'm not sure that it really got that much focus

458
00:20:33.860 --> 00:20:34.720
in the campaign.

459
00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:37.770
Maybe that was intentional, maybe not, I don't know.

460
00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:41.290
But that's the story that I think my audience wants to hear.

461
00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:43.380
And I think it's so powerful.

462
00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:44.213
It's so true.

463
00:20:44.213 --> 00:20:49.210
And nothing will impact a family more than health,

464
00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:53.670
things we call a chronic disease and the sick care

465
00:20:53.670 --> 00:20:58.670
that we basically believe we have normalized sick care.

466
00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:01.800
We don't have healthcare, we have sick care.

467
00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:05.667
And I was the victim of that at 54, 55,

468
00:21:07.970 --> 00:21:12.970
I received the diagnosis that I was experiencing

469
00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:16.660
late stages of diabetes.

470
00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:17.810
Cause vision loss.

471
00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:20.060
I woke up 'cause I couldn't see the alarm clock

472
00:21:20.060 --> 00:21:22.440
'cause my left eye was just shocked.

473
00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:23.710
And the doctor said, "Listen,

474
00:21:23.710 --> 00:21:25.790
you're gonna lose your sight in a year Eric."

475
00:21:25.790 --> 00:21:28.670
And had permanent nerve damage in my hands and feet.

476
00:21:28.670 --> 00:21:30.470
They were tingling all the time.

477
00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:32.423
I thought it was just falling asleep.

478
00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:35.870
I was overweight, did not realize that

479
00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:38.090
because I looked fine to me.

480
00:21:38.090 --> 00:21:41.800
But throughout the year, as you say I'm in my mid 50s.

481
00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:42.633
Filling out.

482
00:21:42.633 --> 00:21:43.466
Yeah right.

483
00:21:43.466 --> 00:21:44.299
(laughs)

484
00:21:44.299 --> 00:21:45.227
Yes and--

485
00:21:45.227 --> 00:21:47.770
About 35, 40 pounds heavier?

486
00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:49.800
Yeah about 35 pounds heavier.

487
00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:52.250
And I had this terrible feeling in my stomach.

488
00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:53.930
That's what sent me to doctor in the first place

489
00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:56.210
'cause you know, men, you have to drag us to the doctor,

490
00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:57.579
you suck it out.

491
00:21:57.579 --> 00:21:58.600
It's got to be really bad.

492
00:21:58.600 --> 00:21:59.790
Right, right.

493
00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:01.270
And I thought it was colon cancer

494
00:22:01.270 --> 00:22:03.070
because it was a not that wouldn't move,

495
00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:05.190
it wasn't gas moving around.

496
00:22:05.190 --> 00:22:08.410
And when the doctor checked me, when I came out of sedation,

497
00:22:08.410 --> 00:22:09.700
he checked my colon and my stomach,

498
00:22:09.700 --> 00:22:11.030
he said hey you have an ulcer.

499
00:22:11.030 --> 00:22:13.650
He both, he said, but your real problems is your diabetes,

500
00:22:13.650 --> 00:22:16.400
he says you in late stages.

501
00:22:16.400 --> 00:22:19.910
And I went to five of the best doctors in the city

502
00:22:19.910 --> 00:22:23.880
and they all told me the same thing, that it was hereditary,

503
00:22:23.880 --> 00:22:26.280
that there's not much you can do.

504
00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:28.776
You're going to be on insulin, the rest of your life.

505
00:22:28.776 --> 00:22:30.780
You going to be on medicine the rest of your life.

506
00:22:30.780 --> 00:22:33.472
And that's just, I was like, no.

507
00:22:33.472 --> 00:22:34.305
(laughs)

508
00:22:34.305 --> 00:22:37.350
Because my mom was diabetic for 15 years at the time,

509
00:22:37.350 --> 00:22:40.230
seven years on insulin.

510
00:22:40.230 --> 00:22:42.930
And I just refuse to accept that.

511
00:22:42.930 --> 00:22:44.510
My sister was experiencing,

512
00:22:44.510 --> 00:22:46.310
she lost a kidney through diabetes,

513
00:22:46.310 --> 00:22:49.060
another sister lost a breast to breast cancer.

514
00:22:49.060 --> 00:22:51.320
Another brother was going through cancer as well.

515
00:22:51.320 --> 00:22:54.470
Another brother was dealing with prostate cancer.

516
00:22:54.470 --> 00:22:57.570
So it was, the family was dealing with,

517
00:22:57.570 --> 00:23:00.780
we were at the stage of chronic diseases

518
00:23:00.780 --> 00:23:03.390
that's going to get those notifications one at a time.

519
00:23:03.390 --> 00:23:04.330
But given that,

520
00:23:04.330 --> 00:23:07.320
you have it throughout your family history

521
00:23:07.320 --> 00:23:10.170
and you on some level conscious or otherwise

522
00:23:10.170 --> 00:23:11.600
you're experiencing these symptoms,

523
00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:12.690
you know something is wrong.

524
00:23:12.690 --> 00:23:15.780
And you know, diabetes is probably in the cards for you.

525
00:23:15.780 --> 00:23:18.410
It probably didn't come as that big of a surprise.

526
00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:21.360
That that was something that you were contending with.

527
00:23:21.360 --> 00:23:25.340
Where does that impulse to say, I'm not having this

528
00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.784
